QUESTIONS=[
 'In each case, find the point of intersection P(x,y) of the pair of lines: (a) 2x+4y−10 = 0, 5x−3y+1 = 0; (b) 2x+y−8 = 0, 3x+2y−2 = 0.',
 'Show that the following lines are concurrent. If the lines are concurrent, then find out the point at which the given lines make concurrency: (a) x−y−2 = 0, 2x−y−5 = 0, 11x−5y−28 = 0; (b) x+2y−3 = 0, 2x−y+4 = 0, x+4y−7 = 0; (c) 3x+2y−1 = 0, 2x−3y+4 = 0, x+y−2 = 0.',
 'If ABC is a triangle with vertices A(0,0), B(8,6) and C(12,0), show that (a) the right bisectors of triangle ABC are concurrent; (b) the altitudes are concurrent; (c) the medians are concurrent.',
 'Find the area of the triangular region whose vertices are: (a) P₁(0,0), P₂(2,4), P₃(−2,2); (b) P₁(−1,−2), P₂(2,5), P₃(5,2); (c) P₁(4,−5), P₂(5,−6), P₃(3,1).',
 'Find the area bounded by triangle ABC whose vertices are: (a) A(−3,6), B(3,2), C(6,0); (b) A(−2,4), B(3,−6), C(1,−2); (c) Are the vertices in parts a and b of triangle ABC collinear?',
 'Find two first degree straight lines in x and y when the second degree homogeneous equations are: (a) 3x²−2xy−5y² = 0; (b) 4x²−9xy+5y² = 0.',
 'Show that the two first degree straight lines in x and y are coincident, perpendicular or neither when represented by: (a) x²+5xy−y² = 0; (b) 2x²−xy−y² = 0.',
 'Find a joint equation of the straight line that passes through the origin and (a) perpendicular to the lines represented by 3x²−7xy+2y² = 0; (b) perpendicular to the lines represented by x²−2tanθxy−y² = 0; (c) perpendicular to the lines represented by ax²+2hxy+by² = 0.'
]
STEPS=[
 ['(a) Divide the first equation by 2 to obtain x+2y = 5, so x = 5−2y.','Substitute into 5x−3y+1 = 0: 25−10y−3y+1 = 0.','Thus y = 2 and x = 1. Check: 2+8−10 = 0 and 5−6+1 = 0.','(b) From 2x+y−8 = 0, y = 8−2x.','Substitute into 3x+2y−2 = 0: 3x+16−4x−2 = 0, giving x = 14.','Then y = −20. Check: 28−20−8 = 0 and 42−40−2 = 0.'],
 ['Concurrent lines must share one finite point. Solve two nonparallel lines and substitute into the third.','(a) Subtract x−y = 2 from 2x−y = 5: x = 3, then y = 1.','The third line gives 11·3−5·1−28 = 0, so all three meet at (3,1).','(b) Solve x+2y = 3 and 2x−y = −4: x = −1 and y = 2.','The third line gives −1+4·2−7 = 0, so all three meet at (−1,2).','(c) Solve 3x+2y = 1 and 2x−3y = −4. Elimination gives x = −5/13, y = 14/13.','At this point x+y−2 = 9/13−26/13 = −17/13, which is nonzero.','Thus (c) is not concurrent as printed, despite the request to show concurrency. No source coefficient is silently changed.'],
 ['(a) A point (x,y) on the perpendicular bisector of AB has equal squared distances to A and B: 16x+12y = 100, or 4x+3y−25 = 0.','Equal distances to B and C give 8x−12y = 44, or 2x−3y−11 = 0. The bisector of CA is x = 6.','With x = 6 both other equations give y = 1/3. All three meet at the circumcenter (6,1/3).','(b) BC has direction (4,−6); its altitude through A is 2x−3y = 0. CA is horizontal, so the altitude through B is x = 8.','AB has direction (8,6), giving the altitude through C: 4x+3y−48 = 0. All three contain (8,16/3).','(c) Opposite-side midpoints are (10,3), (6,0), and (4,3). The medians are 3x−10y = 0, 3x−y−18 = 0, and 3x+8y−36 = 0.','Their common point is the coordinate average G = ((0+8+12)/3,(0+6+0)/3) = (20/3,2).','Substitution gives zero in all three median equations. Each center is found from its own defining lines; the three centers need not coincide.'],
 ['Use A = |(P₂−P₁)×(P₃−P₁)|/2 for geometric area.','(a) The two displacements are (2,4) and (−2,2).','Their cross product is 2·2−4(−2) = 12, giving area 6.','(b) The displacements are (3,7) and (6,4).','Their cross product is 3·4−7·6 = −30, giving area 15.','(c) The displacements are (1,−1) and (−1,6). Their cross product is 6−1 = 5, giving area 5/2.','All areas are in square coordinate units. The negative cross product in (b) records orientation, not negative geometric area.'],
 ['Apply half the absolute cross product of AB and AC.','(a) AB = (6,−4) and AC = (9,−6).','The cross product is 6(−6)−(−4)9 = −36+36 = 0, so area is 0.','(b) AB = (5,−10) and AC = (3,−6).','The cross product is 5(−6)−(−10)3 = −30+30 = 0, so area is 0.','(c) Both cross products vanish, so each triple is collinear and forms a degenerate triangle.','As a second check, part (a) points lie on 2x+3y−12 = 0 and part (b) points lie on 2x+y = 0.'],
 ['(a) Look for factors of 3x²−2xy−5y².','The product (x+y)(3x−5y) expands to 3x²−5xy+3xy−5y².','Combining the middle terms gives the exact source polynomial.','Therefore the two lines are x+y = 0 and 3x−5y = 0.','(b) The product (x−y)(4x−5y) expands to 4x²−5xy−4xy+5y².','This is 4x²−9xy+5y², so the lines are x−y = 0 and 4x−5y = 0.','All factors are nonzero linear forms; each product equation is precisely the union of its two lines through the origin.'],
 ['For Q = ax²+2hxy+by², compute D = h²−ab. A real pair is coincident when D = 0 and perpendicular when a+b = 0 with D > 0.','(a) a = 1, h = 5/2, b = −1 gives D = 25/4+1 = 29/4 > 0.','Thus the lines are distinct. Their equations are x+((5+√29)/2)y = 0 and x+((5−√29)/2)y = 0.','Since a+b = 0, they are perpendicular, not coincident.','(b) Factor 2x²−xy−y² = (x−y)(2x+y).','The two slopes are 1 and −2; they are different and their product is −2.','Therefore the lines in (b) are neither coincident nor perpendicular. The coefficient checks D = 9/4 > 0 and a+b = 1 give the same conclusion.'],
 ['For a line pair through the origin, rotate both lines through 90° about the origin to obtain their perpendicular pair.','If the original point coordinates in Q are replaced by (−y,x), then Q(−y,x) = bx²−2hxy+ay² describes the rotated pair.','(a) With a = 3, 2h = −7 and b = 2, the new joint equation is 2x²+7xy+3y² = 0.','Check: the original factors are (3x−y)(x−2y); perpendicular factors are (x+3y)(2x+y), whose product is the new equation.','(b) With a = 1, h = −tanθ and b = −1, the rotated equation is −x²+2tanθxy+y² = 0.','Multiplying by −1 gives x²−2tanθxy−y² = 0, the same pair. This occurs because the original real lines are already perpendicular. Require tanθ to be defined.','(c) The general result is bx²−2hxy+ay² = 0. Rotation also handles a vertical line without dividing by its slope.','For two real lines, require a nonzero quadratic and h²−ab ≥ 0. If the discriminant is negative, the source does not represent a real line pair to which real perpendicularity applies.']
]
ANSWERS=['(a) (1,2); (b) (14,−20).','(a) concurrent at (3,1); (b) concurrent at (−1,2); (c) not concurrent as printed.','(a) circumcenter (6,1/3); (b) orthocenter (8,16/3); (c) centroid (20/3,2).','(a) 6; (b) 15; (c) 5/2 square units.','Both areas are 0; both triples are collinear.','(a) x+y = 0, 3x−5y = 0; (b) x−y = 0, 4x−5y = 0.','(a) distinct perpendicular lines; (b) neither coincident nor perpendicular.','(a) 2x²+7xy+3y² = 0; (b) x²−2tanθxy−y² = 0; (c) bx²−2hxy+ay² = 0.']
